WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.080
So, my science is basic science

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.850
and what that means is that i'm finding out

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.160
how something works at a very fundamental level.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.980
You know the physiology of it, the morphology of it,

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:12.540
the mechanics of it.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.080
Whether it ends up at some point in time

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:20.440
helping to solve a problem? We don't know.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:24.119
Maybe. Maybe not. But what it does

00:00:24.119 --> 00:00:27.379
is that it contributes to this base of knowledge

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:29.780
that we have without which we

00:00:29.789 --> 00:00:32.279
would not be able to solve problems at all.

00:00:32.279 --> 00:00:34.200
OK, so science is not a linear process

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.840
it's not that if I want to cure cancer

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.660
you know the easiest way is to start from

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.360
A to B to Z.  It doesn't work that way.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:44.940
You need to have people who are having a

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:48.450
very broad base you know people who are

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:50.219
coming at it from different ways asking

00:00:50.219 --> 00:00:51.420
different questions and then somebody

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:52.800
else comes in and they make an

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.340
unexpected connection.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:58.199
And as you build on that eventually you know

00:00:58.199 --> 00:01:00.319
somebody comes up and they're like:  "Oh yeah

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:01.940
this therapy that they're using

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:04.100
for something totally unrelatable

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.859
might be the key to study this question."

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:10.260
And that's just how it goes and so without

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:13.320
that broad base of knowledge the tip of the iceberg,

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.420
which is finding those applications,

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:17.640
would just simply go away.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:20.580
And so we can't pick and choose from the beginning

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.540
and say: "Well, we're only going to study things

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:25.120
that we know are going to have some benefits.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:26.160
Because we don't know.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:27.080
We don't know what we don't know.

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:28.259
That's the whole point.

00:01:28.259 --> 00:01:30.270
That's the whole point of science.

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:31.860
And in the meantime we're pushing the boundaries

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:34.170
of our knowledge and just figuring out, okay,

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:36.210
so then how do things work you know?

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:39.570
And that's important.

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:41.890
It's an important part of what makes us human i think.

